# Cargo
/target
**/target/

# NOTE: Cargo.lock is committed on purpose. This workspace produces
# executables (the `ntfs-mac` CLI and the `ntfs-mac.app` GUI), and Cargo's
# guidance is to commit the lock file for anything that ships a binary.
# The release build, `cargo audit`, `cargo deny` and the generated
# THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md inventory are all derived from it, so leaving it
# out makes those steps unreproducible. Published library crates ignore it
# regardless, so this does not affect crates.io consumers.

# Tauri
#
# NOTE: `crates/ntfs-mac-tauri/src/` is the hand-written GUI frontend
# (`index.html`, `app.js`, `styles.css`) and is what
# `build.frontendDist: "../src"` in tauri.conf.json points at. It used to
# be ignored here, which meant the repository shipped without the GUI
# source: neither a fresh clone nor CI could build ntfs-mac.app.
# Nothing extra is ignored for Tauri — `target/` is covered above, and
# `crates/ntfs-mac-tauri/dist/` by the `dist/` rule below.

# Node
node_modules/

